# Section 2: Components and Necessary Files

Our Final Grade Calculator will consist of four major components:

1. User Interface Component.
2. Grade Calculation Component.
3. Course Management Component.
4. Database Component.

Each component will perform specific responsibilities within the application.

## 2.1 User Interface Component

**Purpose:**

The User Interface Component allows students to interact with the Final Grade Calculator.

Students will be able to enter course information, submit assignment grades, and view calculated results.

**Subcomponents:**

- Course information input.
- Assignment grade input.
- Current course grade display.
- Required final examination score display.
- Estimated final grade display.

**Necessary Files:**

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| index.html | Provides the main application webpage. |
| style.css | Controls the appearance and layout of the application. |
| script.js | Handles frontend interactions and user input. |

**Database Usage:**

The User Interface Component will communicate with the backend application through application requests. It will not connect directly to the MySQL database.

The backend will retrieve and return the information needed by the user interface.

## 2.2 Grade Calculation Component

**Assigned Team Member:** Jalen Davis

**Purpose:**

The Grade Calculation Component is responsible for performing the mathematical calculations required by the Final Grade Calculator.

It will process assignment scores, grading weights, and course information to determine student grades.

**Subcomponents:**

- Current grade calculator.
- Weighted grade calculator.
- Required final examination score calculator.
- Estimated final course grade calculator.
- Grade validation.

**Necessary Files:**

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| GradeCalculator.java | Contains the primary grade calculation logic. |
| GradeCalculationService.java | Processes grade calculation operations. |
| GradeCalculationController.java | Handles requests related to grade calculations. |
| GradeRepository.java | Provides access to stored grade information. |

**Database Usage:**

The Grade Calculation Component will retrieve assignment scores and grading information from the shared MySQL database.

It will use this information to calculate current course averages and determine the scores required on final examinations.

## 2.3 Course Management Component

**Assigned Team Member:** Malachi Johnson

**Purpose:**

The Course Management Component manages the course information and assignment details entered into the application.

**Subcomponents:**

- Course creation.
- Course information management.
- Assignment management.
- Grading category management.
- Course information validation.

**Necessary Files:**

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| Course.java | Represents course information. |
| Assignment.java | Represents assignment information. |
| CourseService.java | Handles course management operations. |
| CourseController.java | Handles course-related application requests. |
| CourseRepository.java | Retrieves and stores course records. |

**Database Usage:**

The Course Management Component will use the shared MySQL database to store and retrieve course information.

It will also maintain relationships between courses and their associated assignments.

## 2.4 Database Component

**Purpose:**

The Database Component is responsible for storing, organizing, and retrieving information used by the Final Grade Calculator.

Our application will use a shared MySQL relational database.

**Subcomponents:**

- Course records.
- Assignment records.
- Grade records.
- Database connection management.
- Data retrieval and storage.

**Necessary Files:**

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| DatabaseConfig.java | Configures database connectivity. |
| CourseRepository.java | Provides access to course records. |
| AssignmentRepository.java | Provides access to assignment records. |
| application.properties | Contains database and application configuration. |

**Database Usage:**

The database will be shared across the application.

The User Interface, Grade Calculation, and Course Management components will access information through the backend application and its data access layer.

This design avoids maintaining separate databases for individual application components.

