# Architecture Conclusion

The proposed architecture for the Final Grade Calculator will use a three-tier architecture consisting of a presentation layer, application layer, and data layer.

Java and Spring Boot will support backend development, while HTML, CSS, and JavaScript will provide the user interface. MySQL will serve as the shared relational database, and Docker will package the backend application for cloud deployment.

The User Interface Component will allow students to interact with the application. The Grade Calculation Component will process student grades, while the Course Management Component will manage course and assignment information. The Database Component will provide centralized storage for application information.

This architecture will provide an organized foundation for developing the Final Grade Calculator while supporting maintainability, scalability, and future improvements.

The proposed design will also allow the application to be deployed in a cloud environment where students can access its features through a web browser.
